// The host's page size: 16 KiB on macOS (Apple Silicon's; Intel's 4 KiB pages are also covered by it), on Linux the
// auxiliary vector's AT_PAGESZ (6), which follows the environment vector's NULL (4 KiB on x86-64, 4, 16 or 64 KiB
// on AArch64; read only where the program owns its start, so the vector is where the environment ends). Elsewhere
// the largest, 64 KiB: rounding inward to more than
