// ---- Parallel mark (ABLA_GC_WORKERS=n, off by default) ---------------------------------------------------------------
// The mark of __ablaRuntimeHostTraceMarkedAllocations on n threads (the collecting thread and n - 1 started for the mark):
// each claims an object by a compare-and-swap of its state word (layout -> layout + 16; the loser of a race leaves it),
// keeps a stack of its own claimed headers (4,096 entries), and gives half of it to a shared pool (the collection's work
// list, under a spin lock) when the stack fills or when another thread has run dry; a thread with nothing takes from the
// pool, and the mark is over when no thread is busy and the pool is empty. The page directory answers every candidate
// (the lazy registry lookup switches a global mode on its first interior pointer: no race-free form), through a page
// cache of each thread's own. Nothing here allocates or touches thread-local storage: a thread the runtime did not
// register runs it. The sweep stays as it is, on the collecting thread.
